  "metadata": {
    "title": "Tapered-spring finite element models and experimental results",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.14998785",
    "publication_date": "2025-03-10",
    "description": "<p>Input and output files for Abaqus CAE finite element models, and experimental moment-rotation results, discussed in \"Fold propagation in tapered-springs: Part I\" and \"Fold propagation in tapered-springs: Part II\", <em>Proceedings of the Royal Society of London. Series A: Mathematical, Physical and Engineering Sciences.&nbsp;</em></p>\n<p>Input files (.py) should be run as scripts in Abaqus CAE.&nbsp;Experimental data csv provides angles in degrees and moments in Nm. M1 corresponds to the torque gauge at the left end of the spring, and M2 at the right end.</p>",
